### INSTANT-SEARCH — the web client's menu search box
###
### This file lints cleanly with no backend. It demonstrates the `INSTANT-SEARCH` verb, the
### `EXPECT InstantSearch.*` subjects, and `OPEN-ROW InstantSearch`.
###
### `INSTANT-SEARCH <text>` calls the server's instant search (the app's Advanced.HandleInstantSearch,
### behind the `Instant?q=` endpoint) and CAPTURES the result rows. Like CHART it is a read-only
### observable, NOT a navigation destination:
###   • no frame is pushed, and
###   • the capture is cleared by the next executable verb (EXPECT doesn't clear it).
###
### Instant search is per user: the server turns it on via Advanced.GetInstantSearchDelayForUser. When
### it is off, INSTANT-SEARCH fails with state-instant-search-off — gate on `InstantSearch.Enabled`.
###
### The live round-trip is exercised by Vidyano.Script.IntegrationTests (InstantSearchTests), whose
### in-process ShopAdvanced returns the Products whose Name contains the text.

@app = "https://demo.vidyano.com"

SIGN-IN admin / admin
REQUIRES InstantSearch.Enabled = true                    ## skip the rest when the server has it off

### Search, then assert on the rows. Each row has Label (the PO type's label), Breadcrumb (the display
### text), ObjectId, and Id (the PO type id).
INSTANT-SEARCH "g"
EXPECT InstantSearch.Count = 3
EXPECT InstantSearch[0].Label = "Product"
EXPECT InstantSearch[0].Breadcrumb = "Gadget"
EXPECT NavStack.Depth = 0                                ## the search pushed nothing

### The text is a value expression, so it interpolates.
@term = "giz"
INSTANT-SEARCH "{{term}}"
EXPECT InstantSearch[0].ObjectId = "3"

### Open a result's PersistentObject — by index, or by a strict WHERE on one of the row fields.
OPEN-ROW InstantSearch 0
EXPECT NavStack.Top.Kind = "PersistentObject"
EXPECT Name = "Gizmo"

INSTANT-SEARCH "widget"
OPEN-ROW InstantSearch WHERE ObjectId = "1" AS @widget
EXPECT Name = "Widget"

### The capture is per-verb: once another verb runs, the rows are gone.
GO-BACK
EXPECT InstantSearch.Count IS NULL
